 "description": "Faithful replication of Malewczyk, Taraszkiewicz & Czyż (2022), \"Preferences of the Facade Composition in the Context of Its Regularity and Irregularity\", Buildings 12:169. Participants see five visualisations of the same multi-family building whose window composition runs from regular to irregular, and put them in order from the prettiest (1) to the ugliest (5); then they answer gender, age and education. The five pictures are the authors' Blender renders printed as Figure 3 of the open-access paper (CC BY 4.0), used with credit for research; the template is removed if the authors object.\n\nDifferences from the original study: (1) the facades are labelled with neutral letters (Facade A–E) in a random order per participant rather than the paper's numbering; (2) ranking is done by tapping pictures in order instead of the original online form; (3) age is asked in the paper's bands rather than as an open number; (4) the paper's further discussion questions are not included.",
